{"name":"Pastoral","hex":"#edfad9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pastoral","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to shepherds or herders of other livestock.","Relating to rural life and scenes, in particular of poetry."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A poem describing the life and manners of shepherds; a poem in which the speakers assume the character of shepherds; an idyll; a bucolic.","A cantata relating to rural life; a composition for instruments characterized by simplicity and sweetness; a lyrical composition the subject of which is taken from rural life."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pastoral"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pastoral","blocks":[{"text":"The pastoral genre of literature, art, or music depicts an idealised form of the shepherd's lifestyle – herding livestock around open areas of land according to the seasons and the changing availability of water and pasture. The target audience is typically an urban one. A pastoral is a work of this genre. A piece of music in the genre is usually referred to as a pastorale."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Boucher_-_Daphnis_and_Chloe%2C_1743.jpg/330px-Boucher_-_Daphnis_and_Chloe%2C_1743.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pastoral","wikidata":"Q390001"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Giulio_Campagnola_shepherd.jpg/500px-Giulio_Campagnola_shepherd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Giulio_Campagnola_shepherd.jpg/500px-Giulio_Campagnola_shepherd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Young Shepherd, engraving using stipple technique, by Giulio Campagnola, c. 1510","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGiulio_Campagnola_shepherd.jpg